From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: retain Matisse firmware display supply at handoff

The native profile intentionally uses firmware-powered TC358764 until its
complete supply/reset wiring is represented. Enabling a boot simplefb
consumer makes its existing L5 vote subject to regulator_disable() when
MSM removes the firmware aperture. Neither the DSI host nor its PHY adopts
L5, leaving no consumer after handoff. A black physical display was
observed despite active native scanout; supply handoff is under test.

Keep the existing 1.2 V L5 supply enabled in this diagnostic native profile.
Do not change its voltage or invent a bridge pin assignment. This explicit
firmware-power limitation must be removed once native bridge supplies and
suspend sequencing have been validated.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts
@@ -7,6 +7,11 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&pm8226_l5 {
+	/* Firmware-powered display: retain the old simplefb supply vote. */
+	regulator-always-on;
+};
+
 &mdp_smmu {
 	status = "okay";
 };
